-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lex_splices_err_raw_delimiter.pcpp - Lexical: a splice in a raw delimiter

  Break step of lex_splices: a raw string's delimiter is never spliced (as
  in clang), so a backslash in it is a character a delimiter may not hold,
  LX0010, at the raw string. The marked line ends in the splice, so its
  marker is a block-comment marker.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_splices_err_raw_delimiter;

/*
  @@test
    kind error
  @@end
*/

begin
  println(/* // ERROR LX0010@39 // */ R"x\
y(a)x\
y");
end.
